          "line": 208,
          "end_line": 213
        }
      ],
      "mechanism": "The DLL fatally refuses a HEALTH/TIMED NEED_DRAW for every person, an aircraft with class zero, and a vehicle without burn flags or current health because the EECH reference did not draw for these. Both aircraft update sites also suppress TIMED entirely for class zero. These are the physical eligibility rules claimed as moved. A by-value host that legitimately models stochastic bleeding (PERSON, positive level, returns NEED_DRAW then eligible/rolled/hit and a lower level) is stopped before its one sample; an aircraft model cannot decide timed eligibility independently of classification. This is a host-authority/generic-host defect, not evidence of a wrong reference probability.",
      "bounded_correction": "Keep these default eligibility rules in cmb_step.c, ask TIMED at the existing aircraft observer point even for class zero, and restrict the DLL to operation/shape, one-draw, consistency and safe-application validation. Preserve reference no-draw behavior and exact RNG position through host answers. Add production-bridge controls accepting a generic positive-health PERSON timed draw and a class-zero aircraft TIMED answer, while retaining non-TIMED draw, second-draw and inconsistent-answer refusals. Do not alter unchanged DAMAGE math/schema in this correction. Replace bad_health_person_draw with a genuinely invalid protocol case if that request is accepted; a reference-specific no-draw behavior is not itself malformed."
    },
    {
      "id": "TIMED-DOCS",
      "priority": "P3",
      "title": "State the actual provider trigger and critical_late scope",
      "locations": [
        {
          "path": "C:/Users/starscream/Documents/ChatGPT/Enemy Engaged DCS/d2-sensor-detections/eech-campaign/docs/m5-combat-extraction.md",
          "line": 231,
          "end_line": 233
        },
        {
          "path": "C:/Users/starscream/Documents/ChatGPT/Enemy Engaged DCS/d2-sensor-detections/eech-campaign/crates/eech-world/lua/aim-provider.lua",
          "line": 43,
          "end_line": 46
        },
        {
          "path": "C:/Users/starscream/Documents/ChatGPT/Enemy Engaged DCS/d2-sensor-detections/eech-campaign/crates/eech-world/csrc/cmb_step.c",
          "line": 20,
          "end_line": 23
        }
      ],
      "mechanism": "bad_health_hit_ineligible corrupts the first completed TIMED answer with eligible=false (aim-malformed.lua:32); it does not require a timed hit. Only bad_health_fatal at line33 requires hit=true. The step3 evidence text also says DAMAGE answers remain reference, but critical_late changes initial_damage_level for DAMAGE at aim-provider.lua:260-261, affecting its critical_before/after classifications. The kernel header still lists timed health rolls as not moved despite the new HEALTH implementation.",
      "bounded_correction": "Describe the ineligible-answer and actual-hit triggers separately; declare critical_late changes HEALTH and DAMAGE critical classifications (while leaving capability arithmetic/reference forecasts intact); update the stale kernel remainder comment. These are prose/comment corrections without a native rerun."
    }
